  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Mineral Springs Park packs an old arboretum's worth of trees into four acres — a very technical, very short course where 18 holes play at par 54 across manicured pathways. It's the Seattle course that proves you don't need length to need accuracy.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach 3 baskets, the course winds through and around the trees with dual tees and dual baskets on several holes. Newly boundaried and well maintained, it's a favorite for lunch-break rounds and putter practice.",
    "Bring a putter, a midrange, and a lot of patience. Every hole is a corridor, and every corridor is tighter than it looks."
  ],
