  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 15 is the longest at Mineral Springs at 321 feet — still a par 3, still tight, but the one hole where the arboretum's trees demand your full attention from tee to basket. It's the perfect summary of the course: short on paper, sneaky in person, and deeply rewarding when you thread the needle.",
  "localTips": "Bring a putter and a midrange — distance is never the issue here. Dual tees and baskets on several holes mean you can make the round your own. Free to play in an old arboretum on manicured pathways; a great lunch-break round.",
